  "reason": "RNA multiprofile models are much stronger than single-profile baselines, and scvi_n200 currently outperforms pca_n2000 for both single-profile and multiprofile avgpool settings. However, the transformer aggregation gain over avgpool is small for scvi, so it is unclear whether aggregation matters generally or only interacts with the encoder. config_003 tests pca_n2000 with multiprofile and transformer aggregation, directly comparing to config_002 for aggregation and to config_006 for encoder choice. This is the best next experiment because it completes the simple RNA-only 2x2 comparison, isolates important representation and aggregation effects without adding multimodal complexity, and helps decide which RNA setting to use before testing fusion."
